 "notes": "ALP dark-matter decay (phi->2 photons, q=2) search with WINERED spectrograph on Magellan, targeting dSphs Leo V and Tucana II. Headline curve = bottom panel of Fig.1 (ga_sub-crop.pdf), the continuum-subtracted \"line\" analysis; taken directly from ancillary file gagg_line.txt. The plotted \"This work\" red band is the generalized-Hernquist-profile result; I report its lower edge = column 2 (max D-factor), i.e. the boundary of the drawn excluded (red) region, which gives the strongest reach (~7-15e-12 GeV^-1 over 1.8-2.7 eV, matching the abstract characterization of one of the most stringent decay-rate limits). Values binned into ~90 mass bins (median per bin) to tame the spiky per-pixel curve (spikes at edges from atmospheric-transmission gaps are real, e.g. first bin ~1.2e-10 near 1.83 eV). Alternative choices: the conservative min-D-factor edge (col3, ~1e-10, the gray \"excluded even in gen. Hernquist\" boundary, = abstract 10^-10) and the NFW blue band (~2-3e-11, abstract (2-3)e-11) are not reported. 2sigma limit. Limit depends on the assumed differential D-factor (log10 D_LeoV ~ 21.4 for gen. Hernquist) rather than a single local density, so dm_density_assumed is null.",
